# kanso check bugs/type_fn_same_name
#
# SHOULD: refuse the module with the error the same two declarations get
# when they share one file:
#   error[name]: the name `run` is already taken
#
# DOES: across two files of one module the type is silently shadowed by
# the function in a.kso, and the only error is
#   error[arity]: no 2-argument arm of `run` (arms take 1)
# pointing at the construction below. In xsv the function was `run argv`
# in cli.kso and the type was a run of equal neighbours in order.kso; the
# message there was "this can be a none and `run` has no arm for it",
# which says nothing about a type.
type run
  first
  last

fn spans xs
  run xs[1] xs[2]
